# IM 1 runs phases 0..15 (two M1s), EI 16..23, the first NOP 24..31. INT
# goes low at phase 18, inside EI, and stays low: the sample at the end of
# EI is masked (EI's one-instruction delay), the one at the end of the
# first NOP takes it, so the INTA cycle follows that NOP (phase 36), not
# EI.
18  int  0
60  int  1
